1
00:00:24,083 --> 00:00:25,083
Sada-e-Sarhad.

2
00:00:26,083 --> 00:00:30,083
The Prime Minister of India
has embarked on a historic journey today.

3
00:00:32,083 --> 00:00:33,750
This bus, brimming with goodwill,

4
00:00:33,833 --> 00:00:36,750
is now heading
toward the Attari-Wagah border.

5
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:38,875
Across the border,

6
00:00:38,958 --> 00:00:41,541
Prime Minister Nawaz Sharif
and his entire cabinet

7
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:44,333
await the arrival of their
Indian counterpart.

8
00:00:44,916 --> 00:00:47,000
And here comes the historic moment.

9
00:00:47,083 --> 00:00:50,333
The bus crosses into Pakistani territory.

10
00:00:50,416 --> 00:00:54,958
Pakistan's Prime Minister,
Nawaz Sharif, welcomes Vajpayee ji.

11
00:00:55,458 --> 00:00:59,125
The prime ministers of both nations
will now receive the Guard of Honor.

12
00:00:59,208 --> 00:01:03,541
The chiefs of Pakistan's armed forces
were expected to attend,

13
00:01:03,625 --> 00:01:06,583
but they appear to be absent
from the event.

14
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:08,416
Sir, isn't this a bit unusual?

15
00:01:11,083 --> 00:01:12,666
Sir, this is such a historic event,

16
00:01:13,291 --> 00:01:17,416
and not one of Pakistan's chiefs from the
Army, navy, or air force, is to be seen.

17
00:01:18,083 --> 00:01:19,750
It is certainly unusual.

18
00:01:21,125 --> 00:01:22,833
But that's expected out of them.

19
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:27,041
Do you know? In the Pakistan Army,

20
00:01:27,125 --> 00:01:31,166
even a colonel gets
five acres of land after retirement.

21
00:01:33,458 --> 00:01:34,708
The country is starving,

22
00:01:35,291 --> 00:01:37,458
and yet half their budget
goes to the military.

23
00:01:37,541 --> 00:01:40,125
When so much is at stake,

24
00:01:40,208 --> 00:01:43,166
do you really think
their army wants peace?

25
00:01:55,541 --> 00:01:57,000
What is the meaning of this stunt?

26
00:01:57,583 --> 00:02:00,416
If the three of you had any objections
to the peace talks,

27
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,000
why didn't you tell me?

28
00:02:03,916 --> 00:02:05,166
And, General Musharraf,

29
00:02:05,958 --> 00:02:10,000
just weeks ago, you spoke of friendship
between Islamabad and Rawalpindi.

30
00:02:13,083 --> 00:02:15,708
My intentions haven't changed, sir.

31
00:02:16,416 --> 00:02:18,333
I'm only concerned about Kashmir.

32
00:02:18,916 --> 00:02:19,958
And I am not?

33
00:02:21,375 --> 00:02:24,208
Why do you think
these peace talks are happening?

34
00:02:25,375 --> 00:02:27,000
Why has Vajpayee sahib come here?

35
00:02:27,083 --> 00:02:29,958
Vajpayee sahib is a poet, sir.

36
00:02:31,416 --> 00:02:33,875
And poetic gatherings won't solve
the issue of Kashmir.

37
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,291
Believe me, sir.

38
00:02:36,375 --> 00:02:39,083
India will only understand
the language of pressure, sir.

39
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:44,583
I made you Chief out of turn, General.

40
00:02:45,958 --> 00:02:48,583
But I forgot
that you have no understanding

41
00:02:48,666 --> 00:02:51,083
of diplomacy or politics.

42
00:02:56,583 --> 00:02:59,208
This evening, all three of you
will be present at the Governor's House.

43
00:03:00,708 --> 00:03:03,416
And you'll also accord Vajpayee sahib
a full state salute.

44
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:04,375
Get that?

45
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:06,083
-Yes.
-Yes.

46
00:03:06,791 --> 00:03:08,041
That's settled, then.

47
00:04:13,208 --> 00:04:15,375
You didn't call before coming…

48
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:18,041
If I had called,
would you have let me come?

49
00:04:19,708 --> 00:04:22,625
Madhavi, I told you,

50
00:04:23,458 --> 00:04:25,583
I needed some time
to talk to your parents--

51
00:04:25,666 --> 00:04:27,916
Bala, they just weren't interested
in talking!

52
00:04:28,875 --> 00:04:31,208
My dad was showing me photos
of four different guys every day.

53
00:04:31,291 --> 00:04:32,791
"This one's in IT. That one's got an MBA."

54
00:04:32,875 --> 00:04:33,750
If I hadn't run away,

55
00:04:33,833 --> 00:04:35,791
they would have forced me
to marry some random guy.

56
00:04:35,875 --> 00:04:38,166
-Yes, I understand, but--
-You don't understand!

57
00:04:38,666 --> 00:04:41,708
I've been telling you for six months
that there's no option.

58
00:04:41,791 --> 00:04:42,708
We have to elope.

59
00:04:42,791 --> 00:04:44,500
That's why I packed everything and--

60
00:04:44,583 --> 00:04:46,500
Landed up at my squadron?

61
00:04:48,375 --> 00:04:51,166
What must all my seniors
and colleagues be thinking?

62
00:04:51,250 --> 00:04:53,791
The annual war exercise is going on.
I'm already struggling.

63
00:04:54,750 --> 00:04:56,416
I mean, you could've at least called
before coming.

64
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:58,166
I'd have figured something out.

65
00:05:01,875 --> 00:05:03,000
Madhavi.

66
00:05:05,250 --> 00:05:06,500
Bala.

67
00:05:10,333 --> 00:05:14,958
I left behind my home, parents, friends,
my entire life in the middle of the night…

68
00:05:17,375 --> 00:05:18,375
just for you.

69
00:05:21,583 --> 00:05:23,791
And you're worried about
what your colleagues will think?

70
00:05:25,583 --> 00:05:26,708
Madhavi, I…

71
00:05:27,958 --> 00:05:28,958
I…

72
00:05:30,416 --> 00:05:31,416
Madhavi…

73
00:05:32,416 --> 00:05:33,416
Madhavi!

74
00:05:38,791 --> 00:05:39,958
Sangy, Goofy in position?

75
00:05:40,041 --> 00:05:41,875
-Sangy in position.
-Goofy in position.

76
00:05:41,958 --> 00:05:43,375
Accelerating to 700.

77
00:05:43,458 --> 00:05:44,708
Sangy, roger.

78
00:05:44,791 --> 00:05:45,791
Goofy, roger.

79
00:05:46,916 --> 00:05:48,041
Baldy, monitor?

80
00:05:48,125 --> 00:05:49,875
Bala, do you love me or not?

81
00:05:51,625 --> 00:05:52,708
Baldy, confirm monitored.

82
00:05:53,958 --> 00:05:54,875
Seven hundred.

83
00:05:56,541 --> 00:05:57,458
Baldy 700.

84
00:05:57,541 --> 00:06:02,166
I left behind my home, parents, friends,
my entire life in the middle of the night…

85
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,958
I've been telling you for six months
that there's no other option.

86
00:06:08,041 --> 00:06:09,458
We have to elope.

87
00:06:09,541 --> 00:06:11,125
Bala, do you love me or not?

88
00:06:11,208 --> 00:06:14,041
Will you run away with me and get married?
Bala. Please understand.

89
00:06:14,125 --> 00:06:15,208
Baldy, abort!

90
00:06:17,375 --> 00:06:18,500
Are you okay?

91
00:06:19,375 --> 00:06:21,458
Yeah, everything's okay.
Let's focus on the formation.

92
00:06:22,041 --> 00:06:23,083
Let's do it again.

93
00:06:23,166 --> 00:06:25,583
-Sangy, Goofy, in position?
-Sangy in position.

94
00:06:25,666 --> 00:06:26,666
Goofy in position.

95
00:06:27,291 --> 00:06:30,791
-Accelerating to 750 now.
-Okay, 750.

96
00:06:30,875 --> 00:06:32,541
Baldy, catch up. Stabilize.

97
00:06:32,625 --> 00:06:34,166
-Let's stabilize at 700.
-Negative.

98
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:35,583
Accelerate to 750.

99
00:06:35,666 --> 00:06:37,583
-Don't accelerate.
-Accelerate to 750.

100
00:06:37,666 --> 00:06:39,458
Goofy, peel off. Sangy, aborting.

101
00:06:41,250 --> 00:06:43,583
What are you doing, man, Sangy?

102
00:06:45,041 --> 00:06:46,708
Sangy, don't abort on your own.

103
00:06:47,666 --> 00:06:48,833
Look at him.

104
00:06:48,916 --> 00:06:51,666
His body's gone stiff.
He's drenched in sweat.

105
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:55,958
That is my complication.
You focus on your wingman.

106
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:58,125
What's this "my wingman," "your wingman"?

107
00:06:58,750 --> 00:07:01,000
Ultimately, we have to fly this formation
together, right?

108
00:07:01,083 --> 00:07:03,208
We've already done
three rounds of chair-flying at 750.

109
00:07:03,291 --> 00:07:05,708
Then we'll do more. And keep at it

110
00:07:05,791 --> 00:07:09,000
until maintaining formation
at higher speeds becomes muscle memory.

111
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:10,125
I hope you're listening, Baldy.

112
00:07:10,208 --> 00:07:11,916
What's the point of doing it
in this condition?

113
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:14,958
Tony and Ahuja sir
are challenging us, Sangy.

114
00:07:15,041 --> 00:07:16,500
Learn to take risks.

115
00:07:16,583 --> 00:07:19,083
Dhali, risks should be calculated.

116
00:07:20,166 --> 00:07:22,166
Otherwise accidents happen.
You better understand this!

117
00:07:23,541 --> 00:07:25,583
Look, I know what happened to your father.

118
00:07:26,291 --> 00:07:28,416
Please, try to put it out of your mind
for a little while.

119
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,208
-All right--
-Don't drag my father into this.

120
00:07:30,291 --> 00:07:32,208
-You're getting me wrong again.
-No, man. He--

121
00:07:32,291 --> 00:07:33,416
Don't get personal with me.

122
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:36,125
-I don't want to understand.
-Not getting personal--

123
00:07:36,208 --> 00:07:37,458
Enough, guys!

124
00:07:40,708 --> 00:07:42,750
At higher speeds,
I struggle to maintain focus

125
00:07:42,833 --> 00:07:43,958
on both formation and instruments.

126
00:07:44,583 --> 00:07:46,916
And now Madhavi is also here.
You all know this!

127
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,583
And please,

128
00:07:50,375 --> 00:07:52,875
let me deal with my problems on my own.

129
00:08:07,250 --> 00:08:11,750
Those who make their home
atop piles of weapons,

130
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:15,083
With peace on their lips
And bombs by their side

131
00:08:15,166 --> 00:08:16,583
A circle of deception

132
00:08:17,791 --> 00:08:21,291
Tell those merchants of death
Loud and clear

133
00:08:21,875 --> 00:08:26,125
Tell those merchants of death
Loud and clear

134
00:08:26,208 --> 00:08:30,166
The world now knows their true face

135
00:08:32,625 --> 00:08:35,666
May their tricks succeed

136
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,916
We will not let them

137
00:08:39,625 --> 00:08:41,375
We won't let war happen

138
00:08:41,458 --> 00:08:43,791
We won't let war happen.

139
00:08:59,416 --> 00:09:02,916
Chief of Naval Staff,
Admiral Fasih Bokhari sahib.

140
00:09:10,333 --> 00:09:14,083
Chief of Air Staff,
Air Chief Marshal Pervaiz Mehdi sahib.

141
00:09:20,583 --> 00:09:24,458
Chief of Army Staff,
General Pervez Musharraf sahib.

142
00:09:54,791 --> 00:09:56,125
How long have you two known each other?

143
00:09:57,291 --> 00:10:01,458
We… used to live in the same building.

144
00:10:01,541 --> 00:10:03,583
Then we went to the same school…

145
00:10:03,666 --> 00:10:06,958
went to the same computer classes,
same tuition classes.

146
00:10:09,583 --> 00:10:11,208
Then he came to the Air Force.

147
00:10:13,791 --> 00:10:15,416
And I also… followed him here.

148
00:10:19,583 --> 00:10:21,458
Now let's see where it goes from here.

149
00:10:22,375 --> 00:10:24,458
Did you two have a fight?

150
00:10:34,041 --> 00:10:35,333
Does Baldy have a sortie tomorrow?

151
00:10:37,083 --> 00:10:38,458
No idea.

152
00:10:39,541 --> 00:10:42,583
We Air Force wives have an unspoken rule.

153
00:10:44,416 --> 00:10:46,708
We don't fight with our husbands
before a sortie.

154
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:48,791
Why?

155
00:10:48,875 --> 00:10:49,958
You know,

156
00:10:50,041 --> 00:10:54,916
a MiG-21 flies at around
900 to 1,000 kilometers an hour.

157
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:56,958
Sometimes even faster.

158
00:10:57,041 --> 00:10:59,916
And there are
over 200 controls in that cockpit.

159
00:11:01,250 --> 00:11:04,958
So, processing all these controls
and their combinations,

160
00:11:05,041 --> 00:11:08,291
they have to take split-second decisons.

161
00:11:09,958 --> 00:11:13,625
In these moments, their brains…

162
00:11:16,250 --> 00:11:18,458
can't have room
for fighting and conflict, can they?

163
00:11:20,666 --> 00:11:25,291
That's why the unsaid rule is
"no fight before a sortie."

164
00:11:26,958 --> 00:11:28,041
So, that means…

165
00:11:30,625 --> 00:11:34,833
So, my feelings will now revolve around
Baldy's sortie schedule?

166
00:11:34,916 --> 00:11:37,958
Everyone has their own way of coping.

167
00:11:39,041 --> 00:11:41,125
Like mine, for instance…

168
00:11:44,833 --> 00:11:46,208
I make a list.

169
00:11:47,541 --> 00:11:48,541
And…

170
00:11:50,791 --> 00:11:53,083
on days when Ajay doesn't have a sortie,

171
00:11:53,166 --> 00:11:55,416
I collate my issues
and argue with him in one go,

172
00:11:55,500 --> 00:11:57,791
sometimes I even throw in a few extras.

173
00:12:03,916 --> 00:12:04,916
Thank you.

174
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:34,125
All I remember
is his Crime Master Gogo impersonation.

175
00:12:34,208 --> 00:12:36,166
-Yeah.
-What was that line again?

176
00:12:36,791 --> 00:12:39,208
"I'll pluck out your eyes
and play marbles with them."

177
00:12:39,291 --> 00:12:41,541
People were rolling with laughter.

178
00:12:41,625 --> 00:12:44,125
No, I was talking about you.

179
00:12:44,208 --> 00:12:45,250
Sardar Mogambo.

180
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:47,833
My Sardar Mogambo
was way better than his Gogo.

181
00:12:47,916 --> 00:12:49,166
Come on, Alka. Come on.

182
00:12:49,250 --> 00:12:51,041
-Both were bad.
-Come on, Alka, stop it.

183
00:12:51,125 --> 00:12:53,750
What are you saying, ma'am?
He forced me into it.

184
00:12:53,833 --> 00:12:54,708
I forced you?

185
00:12:54,791 --> 00:12:56,958
I showed up dressed as Baazigar.
You looked at my costume and said,

186
00:12:57,041 --> 00:12:59,208
"You look like Crime Master Gogo."
Ruined it.

187
00:13:00,375 --> 00:13:03,750
-I do a good Shah Rukh, no?
-I'm so glad you two made it here.

188
00:13:03,833 --> 00:13:05,666
Otherwise, in the forces,

189
00:13:05,750 --> 00:13:07,291
transfer orders arrive
just as friendships begin.

190
00:13:07,375 --> 00:13:08,583
I completely agree.

191
00:13:09,916 --> 00:13:10,958
Thank you, Tony.

192
00:13:11,708 --> 00:13:12,958
You're welcome.

193
00:13:13,041 --> 00:13:17,875
-Yes, Sanjeev?
-Sir, I told him you're busy, but…

194
00:13:20,875 --> 00:13:22,166
It's okay, Sanjeev.

195
00:13:25,791 --> 00:13:28,250
Good morning, sir. Good morning, ma'am.

196
00:13:28,333 --> 00:13:30,166
-Good morning.
-So sorry to disturb you.

197
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,208
Come.

198
00:13:31,291 --> 00:13:32,125
Join us.

199
00:13:32,708 --> 00:13:33,791
No, ma'am. Thank you.

200
00:13:38,041 --> 00:13:41,083
Tony sir, I wanted to discuss something
with you.

201
00:13:52,750 --> 00:13:54,083
Go ahead, Baldy.

202
00:13:56,500 --> 00:14:01,083
Sir, ever since I was a kid,
I wanted to be a helicopter pilot.

203
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
There was this stupid movie,

204
00:14:05,083 --> 00:14:07,541
where I saw the villain
bring down a helicopter with a lasso.

205
00:14:08,916 --> 00:14:10,833
That was the day I told my parents

206
00:14:11,833 --> 00:14:14,708
that I wanted to become a pilot
and I'd never let a plane crash.

207
00:14:17,250 --> 00:14:18,750
And I did become one, sir.

208
00:14:20,333 --> 00:14:21,416
A fighter pilot.

209
00:14:23,791 --> 00:14:25,250
But still, sir…

210
00:14:27,458 --> 00:14:28,833
I don't feel complete, sir.

211
00:14:31,291 --> 00:14:33,416
And for that, I…

212
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,083
I need Madhavi.

213
00:14:41,333 --> 00:14:45,000
Sir, whenever I fly,
all I think about is Madhavi.

214
00:14:45,083 --> 00:14:47,916
And when I am with Madhavi,
all I think about is flying--

215
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,541
Baldy, are you talking
about leaving the Air Force?

216
00:14:50,625 --> 00:14:51,708
No, sir.

217
00:14:54,750 --> 00:14:56,083
Tony sir…

218
00:14:58,458 --> 00:15:00,458
please transfer me
to a Transport Squadron.

219
00:15:01,625 --> 00:15:04,291
It's less risky.
Maybe her parents will then accept me.

220
00:15:07,166 --> 00:15:08,625
Baldy, let's do this…

221
00:15:10,291 --> 00:15:11,791
We'll talk about this later.

222
00:15:11,875 --> 00:15:14,291
Sir, I don't want
my colleagues to suffer because of me.

223
00:15:14,375 --> 00:15:15,625
Specially, in the middle of--

224
00:15:15,708 --> 00:15:19,000
Baldy, sir said he'll look into it.
That'll be all.

225
00:15:25,833 --> 00:15:26,833
Sir.

226
00:15:36,416 --> 00:15:39,583
Mian sahib, first of all, congratulations.

227
00:15:39,666 --> 00:15:41,208
To you too.

228
00:15:41,291 --> 00:15:43,041
The bus trip has been a great success.

229
00:15:43,125 --> 00:15:48,041
My trip succeeded
the moment I met actor Dev Anand.

230
00:15:48,125 --> 00:15:50,125
Yes, Dev sahib was telling me

231
00:15:50,791 --> 00:15:53,666
you once dreamed of becoming
an actor yourself.

232
00:15:54,541 --> 00:15:56,875
Just a passing fancy.

233
00:16:00,666 --> 00:16:02,041
Jaswant sahib, we were thinking

234
00:16:02,125 --> 00:16:05,083
we should set a timeline
for the Kashmir dialogue.

235
00:16:06,500 --> 00:16:08,875
As a starting point,
we'd like to propose the Chenab Formula.

236
00:16:09,958 --> 00:16:11,375
The Chenab River divides

237
00:16:11,458 --> 00:16:14,750
the religious populations of India
and Pakistan almost equally.

238
00:16:15,583 --> 00:16:19,916
That's why we believe
it's the ideal resolution to the conflict.

239
00:16:23,416 --> 00:16:24,500
Sartaj sahib,

240
00:16:25,958 --> 00:16:30,166
before we tackle the bigger issues,
we need to take smaller steps first.

241
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:34,958
Vajpayee sahib sincerely wants to
help Pakistan through its economic crisis.

242
00:16:35,041 --> 00:16:36,750
As a gesture of goodwill,

243
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,541
Vajpayee ji would like to offer Pakistan

244
00:16:38,625 --> 00:16:44,000
a loan of 100 crore rupees
and 40 lakh tons of wheat.

245
00:16:47,166 --> 00:16:48,333
Wheat?

246
00:16:50,625 --> 00:16:54,625
If India doesn't want to discuss
the Kashmir issue,

247
00:16:54,708 --> 00:16:56,125
then say so openly.

248
00:16:56,208 --> 00:16:59,791
Vajpayee sahib has expressed his views
on the Kashmir issue many times.

249
00:16:59,875 --> 00:17:01,875
As long as the Line of Control…

250
00:17:04,083 --> 00:17:05,875
remains a hotbed of terrorist activity,

251
00:17:07,083 --> 00:17:10,041
no meaningful dialogue
on Kashmir can take place.

252
00:17:10,750 --> 00:17:13,916
Let's set the Chenab Formula aside.

253
00:17:15,125 --> 00:17:16,416
Tell us this instead.

254
00:17:17,208 --> 00:17:20,416
What is India's proposal
on the Kashmir issue?

255
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:22,958
Surely you have a plan.

256
00:17:23,541 --> 00:17:28,750
We can establish a timeline
for dialogue on Kashmir.

257
00:17:30,708 --> 00:17:34,375
-But this can't be rushed.
-That means there's no thought.

258
00:17:36,291 --> 00:17:38,041
In India's mind,

259
00:17:38,125 --> 00:17:40,000
this issue carries no weight.

260
00:17:40,083 --> 00:17:41,291
Nawaz…

261
00:17:42,791 --> 00:17:46,541
We invited you here in good faith,
treated you as our honored guests…

262
00:17:46,625 --> 00:17:49,750
And you're talking about loaning us wheat?

263
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:05,875
Sometimes I think you forget
why I pleaded with Jilani sahib

264
00:18:05,958 --> 00:18:08,666
to induct you into politics
in the first place.

265
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:10,541
You and I

266
00:18:11,666 --> 00:18:13,791
entered politics
to protect the business interests

267
00:18:13,875 --> 00:18:16,125
of the Ittefaq Group of industries.

268
00:18:18,583 --> 00:18:20,500
For you and me,

269
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:24,125
politics is still a business.

270
00:18:27,208 --> 00:18:28,958
Your economy is sinking.

271
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,208
You're facing corruption allegations.

272
00:18:34,583 --> 00:18:37,166
You need American dollars.

273
00:18:37,250 --> 00:18:43,208
And America needs you
to improve relations with your neighbor.

274
00:18:45,041 --> 00:18:46,291
Even after everything?

275
00:18:54,583 --> 00:18:55,916
Yes, Nawaz.

276
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:01,458
Even after everything.

277
00:19:05,083 --> 00:19:09,250
You will sign the Lahore Declaration.

278
00:19:10,166 --> 00:19:11,666
You'll do it with a smile.

279
00:19:11,750 --> 00:19:13,791
Just look at it like this…

280
00:19:14,666 --> 00:19:17,791
your unrealized dream of acting in films

281
00:19:19,541 --> 00:19:21,250
will finally come in handy.

282
00:19:22,916 --> 00:19:27,416
Today, Vajpayee ji and Nawaz Sharif
signed the historic Lahore Declaration.

283
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:32,791
Under the declaration, both countries
agreed to peaceful dialogue,

284
00:19:32,875 --> 00:19:37,125
exercise nuclear restraint,
and respect the Line of Control.

285
00:19:37,208 --> 00:19:40,000
in accordance with the Simla Agreement.

286
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:45,708
Just few days left before we take off.

287
00:19:47,666 --> 00:19:50,083
It's the war game finals. Where's Baldy?

288
00:19:50,666 --> 00:19:52,791
We haven't nailed the formation even once.

289
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:55,125
Not even in chair flying.

290
00:19:58,416 --> 00:19:59,375
How's it going, boys?

291
00:19:59,958 --> 00:20:02,666
Just waiting for Baldy, sir.

292
00:20:06,625 --> 00:20:07,958
What do you mean, waiting?

293
00:20:08,708 --> 00:20:09,708
Go find him.

294
00:20:11,208 --> 00:20:12,541
Did you check the library?

295
00:20:12,625 --> 00:20:13,583
No, sir.

296
00:20:13,666 --> 00:20:16,166
I… I'll go check.

297
00:20:20,125 --> 00:20:21,625
-Sir.
-Yeah?

298
00:20:24,416 --> 00:20:25,375
If I may, sir.

299
00:20:27,041 --> 00:20:28,083
Go ahead.

300
00:20:29,083 --> 00:20:30,708
Sir, we're not waiting for Baldy.

301
00:20:31,333 --> 00:20:32,875
Actually, we can't find him.

302
00:20:35,291 --> 00:20:37,291
Don't get me wrong, sir, but…

303
00:20:37,875 --> 00:20:40,708
I think we should replace Baldy
in the finals.

304
00:20:43,875 --> 00:20:45,041
Is that what you think?

305
00:20:45,833 --> 00:20:47,250
Sir, it's a tough call.

306
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:48,416
I agree.

307
00:20:49,333 --> 00:20:51,708
But I'm speaking in the best interests
of the squadron, sir.

308
00:20:54,791 --> 00:20:57,375
I don't think
he is in the right frame of mind for it.

309
00:21:04,083 --> 00:21:05,333
19:30 hours.

310
00:21:06,291 --> 00:21:07,500
Training ground.

311
00:21:08,041 --> 00:21:09,708
Bring your bikes, boys.

312
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:13,000
And Baldy too.

313
00:21:16,416 --> 00:21:17,333
Sir.

314
00:21:29,458 --> 00:21:32,333
Sir, I've managed to get through
to Skardu Army Base.

315
00:21:33,416 --> 00:21:35,083
General Musharraf is on the line.

316
00:21:40,875 --> 00:21:42,458
Long live Pakistan, sir.

317
00:21:42,541 --> 00:21:43,916
Sir, I hope

318
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:47,583
the peace talks amounted to more than
just a recital of Vajpayee sahib's poetry.

319
00:21:47,666 --> 00:21:51,333
General Musharraf.
What am I to do with you?

320
00:21:51,916 --> 00:21:53,458
I only asked for a salute.

321
00:21:54,291 --> 00:21:57,208
Sir, while I was standing
in the salute line,

322
00:21:57,291 --> 00:21:59,291
I realized something about myself.

323
00:21:59,958 --> 00:22:01,750
That, I am a simple soldier, sir.

324
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,750
And I only know how to fight wars.

325
00:22:04,833 --> 00:22:07,708
Why? You don't believe in peace?

326
00:22:09,458 --> 00:22:10,291
No, sir.

327
00:22:11,166 --> 00:22:13,708
And what has trusting in peace
gotten you, sir?

328
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:15,666
Wheat?

329
00:22:16,250 --> 00:22:18,083
I told you before, sir,

330
00:22:18,166 --> 00:22:20,958
India will not understand
the language of peace.

331
00:22:21,041 --> 00:22:24,291
And I'm sorry,
but I can't keep lying any longer.

332
00:22:26,791 --> 00:22:29,583
So, I'd rather adopt a path

333
00:22:30,666 --> 00:22:32,333
that sits right with my conscience.

334
00:22:32,916 --> 00:22:34,333
And what is that path?

335
00:22:34,958 --> 00:22:37,500
I want to revive Mujahideen operations

336
00:22:37,583 --> 00:22:40,750
across the Kashmir Valley
on a much larger scale.

337
00:22:45,083 --> 00:22:46,500
Without my permission?

338
00:22:46,583 --> 00:22:48,083
Sir, you are
the Prime Minister of Pakistan.

339
00:22:49,166 --> 00:22:51,583
Who am I? The entire Army is yours.

340
00:22:53,375 --> 00:22:57,708
I have only one request, sir.
Come up to the mountains.

341
00:22:58,916 --> 00:23:02,833
The fresh air up here
will be good for your heart

342
00:23:02,916 --> 00:23:04,750
and your mind.

343
00:23:11,958 --> 00:23:13,041
Mian sahib?

344
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:16,291
Okay.

345
00:23:18,166 --> 00:23:19,916
I'll come with the ISI chief.

346
00:23:21,125 --> 00:23:22,625
Sir, you should first

347
00:23:22,708 --> 00:23:25,583
see the operation for yourself
and judge it on its merits.

348
00:23:26,250 --> 00:23:28,750
After that,
whether it's the ISI Chief or me,

349
00:23:29,791 --> 00:23:32,291
we'll all be at your command, sir.

350
00:23:32,916 --> 00:23:34,791
Sir, tomorrow morning at ten,

351
00:23:34,875 --> 00:23:37,958
the Pakistan Army
will be waiting for you at the helipad.

352
00:23:43,625 --> 00:23:44,625
Sir.

353
00:23:46,458 --> 00:23:48,208
Will you tell him everything?

354
00:23:50,625 --> 00:23:56,208
General Tauqir, you wanted
the PM's approval for Stinger missiles.

355
00:23:56,291 --> 00:23:59,166
-Yes.
-That time has come.

356
00:24:00,708 --> 00:24:02,041
-General Hassan.
-Sir.

357
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:07,375
Mark all captured posts on the map.

358
00:24:07,458 --> 00:24:08,291
Right, sir.

359
00:24:08,833 --> 00:24:10,416
But keep one thing in mind.

360
00:24:11,708 --> 00:24:14,416
The Line of Control should not be marked.

361
00:24:15,333 --> 00:24:16,416
-Right, sir.
-Right?

362
00:24:28,416 --> 00:24:31,833
Arrows, line up your bikes in formation.

363
00:24:34,083 --> 00:24:35,416
Dhali and Sangy, up front.

364
00:24:38,583 --> 00:24:41,208
Teekay, Goofy, flank.

365
00:24:41,291 --> 00:24:42,833
And, Baldy, center.

366
00:24:42,916 --> 00:24:44,666
And, Max, rear.

367
00:24:46,791 --> 00:24:50,541
Take this rope.
Tie all the bikes together.

368
00:24:50,625 --> 00:24:51,625
Let's go.

369
00:24:53,041 --> 00:24:54,583
Come on. Come on.

370
00:24:54,666 --> 00:24:56,625
There should be no slack in the rope.

371
00:24:57,458 --> 00:24:58,958
Keep the rope tight.

372
00:25:00,791 --> 00:25:01,791
The mission is simple, boys.

373
00:25:02,666 --> 00:25:04,041
This is your starting point.

374
00:25:05,250 --> 00:25:06,708
Take the turn from here

375
00:25:06,791 --> 00:25:10,458
and complete one lap of the ground
in six-formation.

376
00:25:10,541 --> 00:25:12,666
But the rope must not break.

377
00:25:13,875 --> 00:25:19,708
If even one rope snaps,
you come back here, tie it again,

378
00:25:19,791 --> 00:25:21,500
and start all over.

379
00:25:25,875 --> 00:25:27,708
The rope should not break.

380
00:25:34,333 --> 00:25:36,791
Keep it ready, boys.
We'll take it nice and easy.

381
00:25:36,875 --> 00:25:39,250
-Good.
-Sangy, we're going too fast.

382
00:25:39,958 --> 00:25:41,666
Stay with me, stick together!

383
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:44,208
-Max!
-Sangy sir!

384
00:25:44,291 --> 00:25:45,791
-Not that way!
-Turn right!

385
00:25:45,875 --> 00:25:47,333
Sangy, what are you doing?

386
00:25:48,333 --> 00:25:49,291
Man!

387
00:26:14,750 --> 00:26:17,708
-Baldy, catch up!
-I'm doing it, Sangy!

388
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:22,458
Baldy, you are getting ahead,
match the speed.

389
00:26:23,750 --> 00:26:25,083
Oh, man!

390
00:26:38,291 --> 00:26:42,041
Dhali, take it easy. Match 30. 30! 30!

391
00:26:42,750 --> 00:26:44,250
Hey, Dhali, look, man!

392
00:26:44,333 --> 00:26:45,625
Too much wobble.

393
00:26:45,708 --> 00:26:47,375
Sangy, let's do it at 40, come on.

394
00:26:47,458 --> 00:26:48,875
Hey, no. No, hey!

395
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:53,541
Why are you increasing speed suddenly?

396
00:26:53,625 --> 00:26:56,083
How's it sudden?
We'll have more control at 40.

397
00:26:56,166 --> 00:26:58,625
-Thirty is too slow.
-The start should be slow, right?

398
00:26:58,708 --> 00:27:00,791
That's how we get to 40. Can't you see?

399
00:27:00,875 --> 00:27:02,708
We've got to get comfortable
with the pace.

400
00:27:02,791 --> 00:27:05,791
Yeah, but you can't be the only one
getting comfortable, we all have to.

401
00:27:05,875 --> 00:27:07,708
I told him before pushing it to 40.

402
00:27:07,791 --> 00:27:09,000
If he's not able to get comfortable--

403
00:27:23,291 --> 00:27:25,416
This squadron will win the war game final?

404
00:27:30,375 --> 00:27:32,375
If you can't hold
a bike formation on the ground…

405
00:27:35,208 --> 00:27:37,083
how are you going to hold
flight formation in the air?

406
00:27:38,208 --> 00:27:39,333
And you…

407
00:27:40,708 --> 00:27:44,750
…do you think a childhood dream
is enough to make you a fighter pilot?

408
00:27:48,291 --> 00:27:49,833
Do one thing, Baldy…

409
00:27:51,583 --> 00:27:55,416
Forget the transfer application
and submit your resignation.

410
00:27:59,125 --> 00:28:00,583
And get out of here.

411
00:28:01,625 --> 00:28:03,208
The Air Force doesn't need you.

412
00:28:03,291 --> 00:28:04,416
Any of you.

413
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:09,666
People who give up this easily
should have no place in the Air Force

414
00:28:09,750 --> 00:28:12,083
or anywhere in the defence forces.

415
00:28:22,166 --> 00:28:23,916
In fact, just forget about it.
The lot of you.

416
00:28:24,916 --> 00:28:26,458
I'll let Tony sir know.

417
00:28:27,125 --> 00:28:29,291
That this squadron
doesn't have what it takes.

418
00:28:29,375 --> 00:28:33,083
These Arrows are not fighters,
just a bunch of quitters.

419
00:28:41,458 --> 00:28:43,083
We won't give up.

420
00:28:43,166 --> 00:28:45,625
-Yes?
-Yes.

421
00:28:46,166 --> 00:28:47,000
Let's do this.

422
00:28:48,125 --> 00:28:49,791
Come on, boys! Steady!

423
00:28:51,750 --> 00:28:52,583
Yes, boys!

424
00:28:56,416 --> 00:28:58,500
Guys, stop! Stop!

425
00:29:00,375 --> 00:29:02,166
I just can't do this!

426
00:29:04,916 --> 00:29:06,625
Guys, leave me out. I'm the problem.

427
00:29:06,708 --> 00:29:07,750
Please.

428
00:29:11,208 --> 00:29:12,625
Why are you thinking like this, Baldy?

429
00:29:13,416 --> 00:29:15,375
You didn't build your life
on empty dreams.

430
00:29:15,458 --> 00:29:17,083
You spent three years
at National Defence Academy.

431
00:29:17,166 --> 00:29:20,375
Then a year at the Air Force Academy.
You've chased this dream your whole life.

432
00:29:20,458 --> 00:29:22,791
And you earned
every bit of it yourself, Baldy.

433
00:29:22,875 --> 00:29:25,958
So nobody else gets to decide
whether you're a fighter or not.

434
00:29:28,208 --> 00:29:30,750
Sangy, you don't get it. Because of me--

435
00:29:30,833 --> 00:29:31,833
Baldy, listen.

436
00:29:32,666 --> 00:29:35,500
Look, we all know
you've got a lot going on in your life.

437
00:29:38,333 --> 00:29:39,958
But this bike doesn't know that.

438
00:29:42,166 --> 00:29:45,458
So, give the next ten minutes,
just ten minutes,

439
00:29:45,541 --> 00:29:47,666
to all of us and this bike.

440
00:29:48,250 --> 00:29:50,625
Ten minutes. That's all.

441
00:29:53,333 --> 00:29:55,333
Without you, there is no formation, Baldy.

442
00:30:01,875 --> 00:30:02,916
Let's do it at 40.

443
00:30:03,500 --> 00:30:05,583
Now that's a fighter's spirit.
Boys, 40 it is.

444
00:30:05,666 --> 00:30:07,875
-Come on.
-Yes. Let's go!

445
00:30:47,625 --> 00:30:48,875
That was a good warm-up, boys.

446
00:30:50,791 --> 00:30:52,625
Cover your speedometers.

447
00:30:53,750 --> 00:30:56,541
Anyone can do it
while looking at the speedometer.

448
00:30:56,625 --> 00:30:58,416
Now do it without looking.

449
00:31:01,208 --> 00:31:02,208
What's wrong?

450
00:31:03,750 --> 00:31:04,625
Too tough?

451
00:31:05,750 --> 00:31:06,875
Can't do it?

452
00:31:10,291 --> 00:31:12,541
-Dhali?
-We'll do it, sir.

453
00:31:16,791 --> 00:31:17,666
We'll do it.

454
00:31:18,916 --> 00:31:22,000
Arrows, we'll become
each other's speedometers.

455
00:31:23,666 --> 00:31:27,875
We'll look at each other,
and we'll ride on feel.

456
00:32:11,958 --> 00:32:12,958
Well done, boys.

457
00:32:15,375 --> 00:32:17,208
Close formation isn't about fighter jets,

458
00:32:18,125 --> 00:32:19,500
it's about fighters.

459
00:32:27,750 --> 00:32:28,708
And, Baldy,

460
00:32:29,625 --> 00:32:32,000
it is our dreams that define us.

461
00:32:33,500 --> 00:32:35,125
Never stop dreaming.

462
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:41,666
And yes…

463
00:32:43,666 --> 00:32:45,875
The date for the war game finals
has been announced.

464
00:32:47,333 --> 00:32:48,291
But this time,

465
00:32:49,708 --> 00:32:51,375
Tony sir and I will fly with you.

466
00:32:53,583 --> 00:32:55,916
Make us proud in the air, boys.

467
00:32:57,875 --> 00:33:00,291
-Jai Hind, Arrows.
-Jai Hind, sir.

468
00:33:23,958 --> 00:33:25,791
-Long live Pakistan, sir.
-Long live Pakistan.

469
00:33:25,875 --> 00:33:26,875
Long Live Pakistan, sir.

470
00:33:26,958 --> 00:33:30,125
-I hope you had a good trip.
-It was very pleasant.

471
00:33:30,833 --> 00:33:31,708
Sir.

472
00:33:34,208 --> 00:33:37,416
Our brave soldiers have established…

473
00:33:39,291 --> 00:33:42,083
eight posts through
sheer grit and hard work.

474
00:33:42,166 --> 00:33:43,125
As you can see.

475
00:33:43,708 --> 00:33:46,625
From here, the Indian NH1
is in our direct line of sight.

476
00:33:49,416 --> 00:33:52,416
And, sir, look at that, sir.

477
00:33:52,500 --> 00:33:54,500
The highest post in this area.

478
00:33:54,583 --> 00:33:58,125
No one has ever dared
capture it before, sir.

479
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:07,333
And we've named it "Sharif Post", sir.

480
00:34:08,375 --> 00:34:09,708
In your honor.

481
00:34:09,791 --> 00:34:10,791
Thank you.

482
00:34:12,083 --> 00:34:15,125
Exploiting this strategy,

483
00:34:15,875 --> 00:34:18,041
if we infiltrate Mujahideen
into the Valley,

484
00:34:18,125 --> 00:34:22,750
and equip them with advanced weapons,
India will come under immense pressure.

485
00:34:25,833 --> 00:34:28,000
But this is what India's problem is.

486
00:34:28,083 --> 00:34:30,666
-Whenever I talk to them--
-This must remain their problem, sir.

487
00:34:30,750 --> 00:34:34,333
Only then will Kashmir become
a focus of diplomatic talks.

488
00:34:34,416 --> 00:34:37,375
Otherwise they'll keep making us sign

489
00:34:37,458 --> 00:34:40,333
useless papers
like the Lahore Declaration.

490
00:34:40,416 --> 00:34:41,500
All right.

491
00:34:42,208 --> 00:34:43,666
But keep me in the loop.

492
00:34:45,208 --> 00:34:47,625
-And no more surprises.
-Certainly, sir.

493
00:34:49,416 --> 00:34:52,833
Sir, if we want this operation
to be fail-proof,

494
00:34:53,500 --> 00:34:56,583
we'll need to equip Mujahideen
with advanced weapons.

495
00:34:56,666 --> 00:34:59,416
Like rocket launchers
and Stinger missiles.

496
00:35:00,250 --> 00:35:01,458
For that,

497
00:35:02,375 --> 00:35:04,166
we need your permission, sir.

498
00:35:05,416 --> 00:35:06,375
Hassan.

499
00:35:07,291 --> 00:35:08,125
Sir.

500
00:35:15,875 --> 00:35:18,625
One day the world
will witness this historic moment.

501
00:35:18,708 --> 00:35:21,416
How the PM himself
came all the way up here

502
00:35:21,500 --> 00:35:23,958
to boost his soldiers' morale.

503
00:36:05,791 --> 00:36:08,333
Arrow 4, accelerate to 700 and join up.

504
00:36:08,416 --> 00:36:09,666
Roger. Joining up.

505
00:36:12,875 --> 00:36:14,208
In position.

506
00:36:14,291 --> 00:36:15,833
Arrows, maintain formation.

507
00:36:15,916 --> 00:36:17,041
And steady at 700.

508
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:25,208
Arrows, turn left to 053.

509
00:36:32,583 --> 00:36:34,166
Accelerate to 750.

510
00:36:35,416 --> 00:36:36,833
Roger. Accelerating.

511
00:36:42,750 --> 00:36:44,166
Now maintain 750.

512
00:36:44,250 --> 00:36:46,333
750. Going steady.

513
00:36:50,041 --> 00:36:50,958
Looking good, Baldy.

514
00:37:05,583 --> 00:37:07,166
Arrow 1 joining up.

515
00:37:07,250 --> 00:37:08,583
Arrow 2 joining in position.

516
00:37:08,666 --> 00:37:10,291
Welcome to the party, Arrow leaders.

517
00:37:12,416 --> 00:37:13,666
Time to tuck in, boys.

518
00:37:28,833 --> 00:37:30,583
Crossing LoC, maintain formation.

519
00:37:30,666 --> 00:37:32,625
-Thirty seconds away from target.
-Roger that.

520
00:37:32,708 --> 00:37:34,125
Let's rock 'n' roll, boys.

521
00:37:40,625 --> 00:37:42,291
The stage is ready, Arrows.

522
00:37:42,375 --> 00:37:43,958
Time to raise the curtain.

523
00:37:44,041 --> 00:37:46,541
Standby to split in five,

524
00:37:46,625 --> 00:37:51,083
four, three, two, one…

525
00:37:51,166 --> 00:37:52,000
Now!

526
00:38:03,291 --> 00:38:05,375
We have a situation here. It's a decoy.

527
00:38:05,458 --> 00:38:07,000
Scramble interceptors now!

528
00:38:07,583 --> 00:38:11,083
On it. Decoys may have fooled us,
but we won't let them cross the LoC.

529
00:38:11,166 --> 00:38:14,291
Roger that, Raider 2. Let's lock them
and get those ten points.

530
00:38:26,166 --> 00:38:29,791
Flash time, Arrow 2. Cameras on standby.

531
00:38:33,666 --> 00:38:35,500
Red Land, say cheese.

532
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:48,750
Arrow 2, bogey on your tail. Watch out.

533
00:38:50,041 --> 00:38:51,875
Looks like they didn't like our photos.

534
00:38:51,958 --> 00:38:53,708
-Baldy, let's surprise them.
-Roger.

535
00:38:56,666 --> 00:38:58,083
Arrow 2, accelerate.

536
00:39:00,250 --> 00:39:01,833
Standby to lock them.

537
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:07,000
Baldy, let's go faster!

538
00:39:07,083 --> 00:39:08,000
Roger.

539
00:39:24,500 --> 00:39:27,291
Shit. Bogeys on our left. Abort pursuit!

540
00:39:28,666 --> 00:39:30,250
Raider 2, let's go towards them.

541
00:39:30,333 --> 00:39:33,583
Roger that, Raider 1. Let's lock them
and get those ten points.

542
00:39:34,708 --> 00:39:35,875
Arrow leaders, we are safe.

543
00:39:35,958 --> 00:39:38,208
Interceptors are flying towards us
to evade the lock.

544
00:39:38,291 --> 00:39:40,208
Baldy, head on cross.
Let's get on their tail.

545
00:39:40,291 --> 00:39:41,500
Roger.

546
00:39:48,708 --> 00:39:49,750
Gunsight on target, Baldy.

547
00:39:49,833 --> 00:39:51,958
Let's lock them
and get those extra points.

548
00:39:53,375 --> 00:39:56,208
Gunsight on target. I have a lock.

549
00:39:58,458 --> 00:39:59,708
Yes!

550
00:40:02,125 --> 00:40:04,750
Well done, Arrows.
Welcome back to friendly skies.

551
00:40:04,833 --> 00:40:07,708
Boys, we've officially won
the war game exercise.

552
00:40:07,791 --> 00:40:10,083
Once again, your record is flawless, sir.

553
00:40:10,166 --> 00:40:11,958
Thanks to Professor sahib.

554
00:40:12,041 --> 00:40:14,666
Today you saved both the photographer
and the photo album, Baldy.

555
00:40:14,750 --> 00:40:16,041
Thank you, sir.

556
00:40:16,625 --> 00:40:18,583
It was a team effort.

557
00:41:05,791 --> 00:41:06,791
Baldy!

558
00:41:08,541 --> 00:41:11,125
Dhali, you guys carry on. I'll see you.

559
00:41:18,166 --> 00:41:19,833
Madhavi. Come with me.

560
00:41:20,791 --> 00:41:22,375
-Where?
-I want to show you something.

561
00:41:23,333 --> 00:41:25,333
-What?
-Just come. Don't ask.

562
00:41:25,416 --> 00:41:27,083
-Come.
-Hey!

563
00:41:33,916 --> 00:41:35,583
Listen up, everyone.

564
00:41:35,666 --> 00:41:37,333
To the victory of Blue Land.

565
00:41:37,916 --> 00:41:38,791
Kick the tire!

566
00:41:38,875 --> 00:41:40,833
-Light the fire!
-Light the fire!

567
00:41:42,416 --> 00:41:43,666
-Cheers, guys!
-Cheers!

568
00:41:43,750 --> 00:41:45,791
-Well done!
-Cheers, sir.

569
00:41:45,875 --> 00:41:47,083
Sir.

570
00:41:52,166 --> 00:41:53,000
Sorry.

571
00:41:53,083 --> 00:41:55,083
I spoke to you about replacing my wingman.

572
00:41:56,916 --> 00:41:58,166
Dhali.

573
00:42:00,166 --> 00:42:02,500
Every pilot has their own problems.

574
00:42:03,416 --> 00:42:05,291
And their own ways of solving them.

575
00:42:07,458 --> 00:42:08,458
Like your problem.

576
00:42:10,708 --> 00:42:12,458
When do you want to focus on that?

577
00:42:16,625 --> 00:42:18,083
Appreciate the offer, sir.

578
00:42:19,541 --> 00:42:21,583
But I don't need help now…

579
00:42:23,375 --> 00:42:24,375
But thank you.

580
00:42:28,291 --> 00:42:29,916
Everybody needs help, Dhali.

581
00:42:31,041 --> 00:42:33,583
Sometimes with flying,
sometimes somewhere else.

582
00:42:34,791 --> 00:42:38,416
But when you need it, ask for it.

583
00:42:39,291 --> 00:42:40,416
Trust me, Flying Officer…

584
00:42:42,666 --> 00:42:44,000
there is no shame in it.

585
00:43:11,708 --> 00:43:14,208
Alka ma'am told me
about the 200 controls in here,

586
00:43:14,291 --> 00:43:16,000
but not about how cramped it is.

587
00:43:24,500 --> 00:43:25,333
Madhavi.

588
00:43:28,041 --> 00:43:30,750
No one can understand
my dreams better than you.

589
00:43:31,958 --> 00:43:33,416
I was scared.

590
00:43:35,291 --> 00:43:39,833
I thought I had to choose between you…
and this jet.

591
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:44,166
But while flying today, I realized

592
00:43:45,541 --> 00:43:47,666
that in flying, there can only be flying.

593
00:43:49,958 --> 00:43:51,041
And…

594
00:43:53,541 --> 00:43:55,083
on the ground, just you.

595
00:44:00,708 --> 00:44:02,541
And I want both.

596
00:44:10,458 --> 00:44:11,541
Will you marry me?

597
00:44:16,958 --> 00:44:17,791
Cheers, guys.

598
00:44:17,875 --> 00:44:18,958
-Cheers!
-Cheers.

599
00:44:19,500 --> 00:44:20,708
Someone's here.

600
00:44:20,791 --> 00:44:22,750
-Mr. Baldy!
-Look who is here.

601
00:44:23,250 --> 00:44:24,125
Tony sir.

602
00:44:24,208 --> 00:44:25,625
-Jacket!
-Baldy!

603
00:44:27,083 --> 00:44:29,583
-Congratulations!
-Bravo!

604
00:44:31,166 --> 00:44:32,791
-What happened?
-They got engaged.

605
00:44:32,875 --> 00:44:34,166
Oh, my!

606
00:44:34,250 --> 00:44:35,958
-Someone--
-Sir, he's going to get married!

607
00:44:36,916 --> 00:44:38,291
Well flown, well played, pilot!

608
00:44:38,375 --> 00:44:39,750
I'm so happy.

609
00:44:42,125 --> 00:44:43,208
Well played!

610
00:44:43,291 --> 00:44:45,500
-Wonderful.
-Three cheers for Baldy and Madhavi!

611
00:44:45,583 --> 00:44:46,708
-Hip-hip…
-Hurray!

612
00:44:46,791 --> 00:44:49,250
-Hip-hip…
-Hurray!

613
00:45:30,750 --> 00:45:31,791
Tony sir!

614
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:54,833
Come on, boys!

615
00:46:56,875 --> 00:46:59,875
Hey, Umesh, what did you do
with your first paycheck?

616
00:47:00,458 --> 00:47:03,166
Bought a bicycle. Watched a movie too.

617
00:47:04,291 --> 00:47:06,041
Then I sent some money home.

618
00:47:07,166 --> 00:47:10,333
-What's your plan?
-I haven't even thought about it, man.

619
00:47:14,750 --> 00:47:15,583
Umesh!

620
00:47:48,500 --> 00:47:50,291
What's the update, Sartaj?

621
00:47:50,375 --> 00:47:52,208
Sir, the situation
has become very fragile.

622
00:47:52,291 --> 00:47:54,708
Sir, two more patrol parties are missing.

623
00:47:55,291 --> 00:47:58,500
Sir, this no longer seems
limited to a single peak.

624
00:47:58,583 --> 00:48:00,958
Judging by the directions of fire,

625
00:48:01,041 --> 00:48:03,708
there could be
over 100 intruders up there.

626
00:48:03,791 --> 00:48:06,041
And they're spread across
at least eight to ten peaks.

627
00:48:07,333 --> 00:48:09,541
The situation is serious.

628
00:48:10,125 --> 00:48:12,708
National Highway 1
is our main route to Leh-Ladakh.

629
00:48:12,791 --> 00:48:18,500
If they capture more points,
the entire Kargil sector could be cut off.

630
00:48:18,583 --> 00:48:22,750
We can't see anything from below
and they're tracking our every move.

631
00:48:23,333 --> 00:48:24,583
What is Pakistan saying?

632
00:48:24,666 --> 00:48:25,916
They're confused too.

633
00:48:26,875 --> 00:48:29,083
According to them, it's Mujahideen.

634
00:48:30,625 --> 00:48:33,083
Why would Mujahideen
do a takeover like this, sir?

635
00:48:34,833 --> 00:48:36,625
Do you think Pakistan is lying to us?

636
00:48:38,625 --> 00:48:42,291
During peace talks,
I don't think Pakistan would do this.

637
00:48:45,041 --> 00:48:49,333
Sir, to counter their height advantage,

638
00:48:51,291 --> 00:48:52,250
we need the Air Force.

639
00:48:58,458 --> 00:49:00,958
Thank you, sir, for meeting
at such short notice.

640
00:49:01,041 --> 00:49:02,708
I will get straight to the point.

641
00:49:02,791 --> 00:49:04,416
INDIAN AIR FORCE

642
00:49:04,500 --> 00:49:06,208
How many troops can the Air Force

643
00:49:06,291 --> 00:49:09,333
airlift by armed helicopters
to elevated positions

644
00:49:09,416 --> 00:49:10,750
in the Kashmir Valley?

645
00:49:12,958 --> 00:49:14,125
It depends, sir.

646
00:49:14,208 --> 00:49:15,125
On what?

647
00:49:15,208 --> 00:49:19,458
Many factors. Elevation, time of the day,
temperature, weather conditions.

648
00:49:20,041 --> 00:49:22,416
-Where exactly in Kashmir?
-Northern sector.

649
00:49:22,500 --> 00:49:24,041
At 15,000 to 16,000 feet.

650
00:49:24,125 --> 00:49:26,458
15,000 to 16,000 feet?

651
00:49:26,541 --> 00:49:29,708
And how far is the nearest
refueling point from these peaks?

652
00:49:31,041 --> 00:49:32,916
Are these details necessary, sir?

653
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:36,625
Just provide us
with helicopters and pilots,

654
00:49:36,708 --> 00:49:38,000
and we'll handle the rest.

655
00:49:42,541 --> 00:49:43,875
Joshi,

656
00:49:45,166 --> 00:49:48,500
why don't you just tell us straight up
what the actual conflict is?

657
00:49:49,333 --> 00:49:53,208
With a little clarity, the Air Force
will be in a better position to help you.

658
00:50:02,541 --> 00:50:06,291
Sir, this is a map of the Kargil,
Drass, and Batalik sectors.

659
00:50:06,875 --> 00:50:10,958
The patrol parties we sent there
over the last ten days have gone missing.

660
00:50:11,958 --> 00:50:14,500
Intruders have seized advantage
of the height,

661
00:50:14,583 --> 00:50:16,666
and occupied our posts.

662
00:50:17,250 --> 00:50:20,791
And, sir, we still don't know
how many peaks they're holding.

663
00:50:20,875 --> 00:50:24,541
That's why we want to airdrop troops
directly by helicopter

664
00:50:24,625 --> 00:50:26,958
and evict them from those peaks.

665
00:50:29,958 --> 00:50:31,625
This is serious, Joshi.

666
00:50:32,500 --> 00:50:34,041
Very serious.

667
00:50:38,500 --> 00:50:40,166
Fine. Give us some time.

668
00:50:41,250 --> 00:50:43,083
We'll quickly chalk out a plan.

669
00:50:43,958 --> 00:50:45,041
Jai Hind, sir.

670
00:50:45,625 --> 00:50:46,625
Jai Hind.

671
00:50:50,875 --> 00:50:51,708
Chief.

672
00:50:53,041 --> 00:50:54,000
Patney.

673
00:50:55,291 --> 00:50:58,208
It's possible that the Army also
doesn't have accurate information.

674
00:50:59,791 --> 00:51:01,041
What is your suggestion?

675
00:51:01,125 --> 00:51:03,250
Directly sending in helicopters
would be suicidal.

676
00:51:04,416 --> 00:51:09,458
Our helicopters would be flying at their
maximum altitude of 15,000 to 16,000 feet,

677
00:51:09,541 --> 00:51:11,791
right where the intruders
are also positioned.

678
00:51:12,625 --> 00:51:14,083
Not safe, for we…

679
00:51:14,791 --> 00:51:17,875
We don't even know who's there
and what weapons they have.

680
00:51:17,958 --> 00:51:19,208
Sir.

681
00:51:21,125 --> 00:51:22,583
We need eyes in the air.

682
00:51:24,541 --> 00:51:28,250
It's time to call the Golden Arrows.

683
00:51:28,333 --> 00:51:30,083
Come on…

684
00:51:30,166 --> 00:51:31,791
Good, good, good!

685
00:51:31,875 --> 00:51:33,000
Yes!

686
00:51:33,083 --> 00:51:35,333
Superb, Alka. You're doing it.
Second gear.

687
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:38,208
Go, and now release… Stop!

688
00:51:40,208 --> 00:51:41,791
You were supposed to ease off the clutch.

689
00:51:41,875 --> 00:51:44,541
I'm driving a Gypsy,
that's why this is happening.

690
00:51:45,250 --> 00:51:47,458
Why can't we wait for our 800 to arrive?

691
00:51:47,541 --> 00:51:50,958
Because if you can drive a Gypsy,
you can drive anything.

692
00:51:51,541 --> 00:51:52,791
Come on, step-by-step.

693
00:51:52,875 --> 00:51:54,625
Step one, ignition.

694
00:51:56,041 --> 00:51:57,250
Station Commander?

695
00:56:27,125 --> 00:56:32,125
Subtitle translation by: Ragini Shaw

